      "text": "To find the total surface area of the right pyramid, we need to calculate the area of the base and the lateral area (the area of the four triangular faces).\n\n1. **Calculate the area of the base:**\n   The base is a square with side length 10 cm.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of the base} = 10 \\times 10 = 100 \\text{ cm}^2\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the slant height of the pyramid:**\n   The peak of the pyramid is 12 cm above the center of the base, and the center of the base is also the center of the square base. To find the slant height, we need to consider the right triangle formed by the height of the pyramid, half the side length of the base, and the slant height.\n   The half side length of the base is \\( \\frac{10}{2} = 5 \\) cm.\n   Using the Pythagorean theorem:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Slant height} = \\sqrt{12^2 + 5^2} = \\sqrt{144 + 25} = \\sqrt{169} = 13 \\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the area of one triangular face:**\n   Each triangular face is an isosceles triangle with a base of 10 cm and a slant height of 13 cm.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of one triangular face} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{slant height} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 10 \\times 13 = 65 \\text{ cm}^2\n   \\]\n   Since there are four triangular faces, the total lateral area is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Lateral area} = 4 \\times 65 = 260 \\text{ cm}^2\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the total surface area:**\n   The total surface area is the sum of the area of the base and the lateral area.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total surface area} = \\text{Area of the base} + \\text{Lateral area} = 100 + 260 = 360 \\text{ cm}^2\n   \\]\n\nThus, the total surface area of the pyramid is \\(\\boxed{360}\\) square centimeters.",
