      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve the problem of finding the total surface area of the right pyramid with a square base of side length 10 cm and a height of 12 cm from the center of the base to the peak, we can break the problem down into a few steps:\n\n1. Calculate the area of the base.\n2. Calculate the slant heights of the triangular faces.\n3. Calculate the area of the four triangular faces.\n4. Sum the areas of the base and the four triangular faces to get the total surface area.\n\nLet's go through these steps one by one:\n\n1. **Calculate the area of the base:**\n   The base is a square with side length 10 cm.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of the base} = 10 \\times 10 = 100 \\text{ cm}^2\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the slant heights of the triangular faces:**\n   The height of the pyramid is 12 cm, and the slant height \\(l\\) of each triangular face can be found using the Pythagorean theorem. The slant height is the hypotenuse of a right triangle where one leg is half the side length of the base (5 cm) and the other leg is the height of the pyramid (12 cm).\n   \\[\n   l = \\sqrt{5^2 + 12^2} = \\sqrt{25 + 144} = \\sqrt{169} = 13 \\text{ cm}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the area of the four triangular faces:**\n   Each triangular face has a base of 10 cm and a slant height of 13 cm. The area of one triangular face is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area of one triangular face} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{slant height} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 10 \\times 13 = 65 \\text{ cm}^2\n   \\]\n   Since there are four triangular faces, the total area of the four triangular faces is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total area of the four triangular faces} = 4 \\times 65 = 260 \\text{ cm}^2\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum the areas of the base and the four triangular faces to get the total surface area:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total surface area} = \\text{Area of the base} + \\text{Total area of the four triangular faces} = 100 + 260 = 360 \\text{ cm}^2\n   \\]\n\nLet's confirm this with the Python code:\n```python\nimport math\n\n# Given dimensions\nside_length = 10  # side length of the base in cm\nheight = 12  # height of the pyramid in cm\n\n# Calculate the area of the base\nbase_area = side_length ** 2\n\n# Calculate the slant height using Pythagorean theorem\nslant_height = math.sqrt(side_length ** 2 / 4 + height ** 2)\n\n# Calculate the area of one triangular face\ntriangular_face_area = 0.5 * side_length * slant_height\n\n# Calculate the total area of the four triangular faces\ntotal_triangular_face_area = 4 * triangular_face_area\n\n# Calculate the total surface area\ntotal_surface_area = base_area + total_triangular_face_area\nprint(total_surface_area)\n```\n```output\n360.0\n```\nThe total surface area of the right pyramid with a square base of side length 10 cm and a height of 12 cm from the center of its base to the peak is \\(\\boxed{360}\\) square centimeters.",
