      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the total surface area of the right pyramid, we need to calculate the areas of the base and the four triangular faces.\n\n1. **Surface Area of the Base:**\n\n   The base is a square with side length \\(10 \\, \\text{cm}\\). The area \\(A_{\\text{base}}\\) of the base is given by:\n   \\[\n   A_{\\text{base}} = \\text{side length}^2\n   \\]\n   Substituting the given side length:\n   \\[\n   A_{\\text{base}} = 10^2 = 100 \\, \\text{cm}^2\n   \\]\n\n2. **Surface Area of One Triangle:**\n\n   Each triangular face of the pyramid is an isosceles triangle with a base of \\(10 \\, \\text{cm}\\) and a height from the peak to the midpoint of the base, which is \\(12 \\, \\text{cm}\\). To find the area \\(A_{\\text{triangle}}\\) of one triangle, we use the formula for the area of a triangle:\n   \\[\n   A_{\\text{triangle}} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height}\n   \\]\n   Substituting the given values:\n   \\[\n   A_{\\text{triangle}} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 10 \\times 12 = 60 \\, \\text{cm}^2\n   \\]\n\n3. **Total Surface Area of the Pyramid:**\n\n   The total surface area \\(A_{\\text{total}}\\) of the pyramid is the sum of the area of the base and the area of the four triangular faces:\n   \\[\n   A_{\\text{total}} = A_{\\text{base}} + 4 \\times A_{\\text{triangle}}\n   \\]\n   Substituting the calculated areas:\n   \\[\n   A_{\\text{total}} = 100 + 4 \\times 60\n   \\]\n   Simplifying the expression:\n   \\[\n   A_{\\text{total}} = 100 + 240 = 340 \\, \\text{cm}^2\n   \\]\n\nThus, the total surface area of the pyramid is \\(\\boxed{340}\\) square centimeters.",
